# Legacy URLs from the pre-Next static site.
#
# These were `redirects()` in next.config.ts, which static export ignores. Cloudflare
# applies redirects ahead of asset matching, so these win over the built-in .html
# handling and return a proper 301 rather than its 307.
#
# The old config also had a `/:path*.html` catch-all sending everything else to `/`.
# That CANNOT be expressed here: a splat may only appear at the end of the source
# path. Do not try `/:page.html /` as a substitute — Cloudflare splits the source on
# `/` and reads a leading `:` as a whole-segment placeholder, so that rule would match
# `/about` and 301 it to the homepage.
#
# Unmatched legacy .html URLs now return a genuine 404, which Google treats better
# than a blanket redirect to the homepage (it classifies those as soft 404s anyway).
#
# TODO: add any remaining legacy URLs still receiving traffic. Source them from
# Search Console's Pages report, the old host's access logs, or:
#   web.archive.org/cdx/search/cdx?url=<domain>/*&output=text&fl=original&collapse=urlkey
# There is room for 2,000 static rules, so enumerate generously.

/contact.html          /contact   301
/free_quotation.html   /quote     301
/prices_delivery.html  /shipping  301
/about.html            /about     301
/services.html         /services  301
/index.html            /          301
